# Line endings are functionally significant for the installer scripts in
# public/: a .cmd file with a bare LF can behave oddly under cmd.exe, and
# a .sh file with a CRLF shebang line fails outright on Linux/macOS
# ("bad interpreter"). Force both regardless of core.autocrlf, so a
# Windows checkout can't silently reintroduce the wrong ending.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.sh  text eol=lf
